WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.400
Public HTTPS application · Real S3 connection · No fixed sample bucket

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.600
Credential entry is omitted. This session was connected privately with user-entered AWS credentials.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:22.400
The application lists the real CSV / XLSX objects available in the connected bucket.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.400
Select s3-test.csv from the bucket, then import it through the asynchronous pipeline.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:31.600
Django returns a job immediately. Celery and Spark process the file while progress remains visible.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.600
Parsing, partitioning, and paginated results run in the background. Waiting periods are edited for brevity.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.800
Import completed: 3 rows and 3 columns, with a paginated preview.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.000
Browse the remaining row without loading the entire dataset into the browser.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Ask in plain English: replace the email domain and preserve the other columns.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.000
AI plans the edit. Celery and Spark apply it asynchronously to the full table.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.200
The asynchronous job validates the regex and applies it to the table. Waiting periods are edited for brevity.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.400
Completed: example.com becomes demo.org. Names and notes are unchanged.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.400
Use the same prompt box to normalize names and extract a new column.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:12.400
The next instruction uses the current result, preserving the earlier email replacement.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.600
Progress reports each validated editing step while the job runs in the background.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.800
Names are uppercase and FirstName is extracted. The email change is retained.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.800
The model also repeated the earlier domain rule; the visible no-match warning reports that extra step.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.000
The remaining record is also transformed: BOB WANG, bob@demo.org, and BOB.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Ask for category updates without providing a mapping rule, and request clarification first.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.200
The assistant evaluates whether the missing category rules require a follow-up question.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.200
Clarification needed: the assistant asks for category rules and leaves the current table unchanged.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.400
View original: mixed-case names, example.com email addresses, and the original three columns.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:02:01.200
Switch back to the edited table. The source S3 object is never overwritten.
